 "result": "`Config.load_env_prefixed()` in `src/tessel/config.py:126` does this.\n\n- **Prefix:** it takes every env var starting with `TESSEL_` (the default prefix) and strips the prefix. `TESSEL_SECRET_KEY` becomes `SECRET_KEY`.\n- **Type conversion:** each value goes through `json.loads` (the default `loads` argument), so `\"true\"` becomes `True`, `\"5\"` becomes `5`, and JSON lists and dicts are parsed. If parsing raises, the value stays a string.\n- **Nested keys:** `__` splits the key into parts. `TESSEL_DB__HOST` sets `config[\"DB\"][\"HOST\"]`, and missing intermediate dicts are created.\n\nVars are processed in sorted order.",
